frac{x}{x}+\\frac{6}{x})}{(\\frac{x}{x}-\\frac{1}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+1+\\frac{6}{x})}{(1-\\frac{1}{x})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when $x$ is very large, the terms $\\frac{6}{x}$ and $\\frac{1}{x}$ become very small. Therefore, as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{(2x+1+\\frac{6}{x})}{(1-\\frac{1}{x})} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{2x+1+0}{1-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+1}{1} \\\\  & =2x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not a constant, which means that $y=f(x)$ does not have a horizontal asymptote." 13194139535641 true] [17592186358993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358994 13194139535641 true] [17592186358993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358995 13194139535641 true] [17592186358993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358996 13194139535641 true] [17592186358993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358997 13194139535641 true] [17592186358993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358998 13194139535641 true] [17592186358993 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535641 true] [17592186358993 1041 "selection" 13194139535641 true] [17592186358993 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358994 13194139535641 true] [17592186358993 1110 #uuid "c29a19c0-97cf-5dd4-8b8c-375d038c2334" 13194139535641 true] [17592186358994 1034 "No horizontal asymptotes" 13194139535641 true] [17592186358994 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535641 true] [17592186358994 1111 #uuid "14574f5d-9fef-5e0a-84d3-03e5ad3b5644" 13194139535641 true] [17592186358995 1034 "y=0" 13194139535641 true] [17592186358995 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535641 true] [17592186358995 1111 #uuid "1a6efa0d-ca66-5d3f-a810-292a58fcf623" 13194139535641 true] [17592186358996 1034 "y=2" 13194139535641 true] [17592186358996 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535641 true] [17592186358996 1111 #uuid "464da4c9-214a-5940-ab57-8174ac122774" 13194139535641 true] [17592186358997 1034 "y=-2" 13194139535641 true] [17592186358997 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535641 true] [17592186358997 1111 #uuid "ade529c8-7f3a-57e1-8368-45d8f6ac77de" 13194139535641 true] [17592186358998 1034 "y=1" 1319